  "FLINK-33199": {
    "jira_id": "FLINK-33199",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "ArchitectureTests should test for fully qualified class names instead of Class objects",
    "description": "Currently architecture tests rely on importing such classes as MiniClusterExtension. This introduces a production scope dependency on flink-test-utils which in turn depends on flink-streaming-java. This is problematic because adding architecture tests to any direct or transitive dependency of flink-streaming-java creates a dependency cycle.\r\n\r\nExample: https://github.com/apache/flink/pull/22850#discussion_r1243343382\r\n\r\nIn general, since architecture tests are supposed to be used freely in any submodule, it is desirable to reduce its dependency surface as much as possible to prevent such cycles. \r\n\r\nThis can be achieved by moving away from using Class objects and employing fully qualified type names checks instead.",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "3df668cc6b29003d2d62e60fd8ad7f6bdc23c1ec",
        "message": "[FLINK-33199][tests] Use fully qualified class names instead of Class objects in ArhitectureTests",
